 "root_cause": "Window entry points performed their initial database lookups before ownership registration. Close could complete early or a disconnected caller could lose the workflow. Admitted windows then re-entered public transcript admission, allowing shutdown to reject their later read.",
 "changes": [
  "Own full, explicit/latest-source window and transcript-ID window reads before the first I/O",
  "Keep one owned workflow through metadata, object read, parsing and the final existence check",
  "Use private read steps inside admitted workflows so closing cannot reject a later internal read as fresh admission",
  "Reject new read entry points before any database or object call once draining starts",
  "Preserve source/Agent checks, concurrent deletion guard, window formatting/ranges and read-only behavior"
 ],
